  "narrative": {
    "es": "Hoy medimos 13095 pares senal+resultado de Scalp CC (1643 nuevos desde ayer; 37 pendientes, 32 outcomes sin senal propia -- el numero de huerfanos sube pero en proporcion al tamano del dato se mantiene estable, sin senal clara de un problema nuevo de pipeline, vigilar igual). De media, por cada operacion se gana 0.055 veces lo arriesgado, con el intervalo de confianza al 90% (0.037 a 0.073) sin cruzar cero -- el sistema sigue ganando en conjunto, un poco mejor que ayer (0.049). Acierto global 46.2%. La causa principal de los stops sigue siendo un objetivo demasiado cerca del stop (RR-bajo), que hoy se despega con claridad como la causa dominante en BUY RETEST (antes casi empatada con otra causa). La gestion con escalera y parciales sigue ganando mas que la simple (+0.074 de diferencia). Hallazgo mas importante del dia: el segmento 1m BUY RETEST paso a tener un edge estadisticamente real por primera vez (antes el intervalo de confianza rozaba cero), sumandose a 5m como los dos segmentos LONG con evidencia solida. Sobre la escalera de ejecucion: seguimos en asesoria (peldano 0) -- el 5m BUY RETEST cumple los cuatro numeros minimos del gate, pero de las dos semanas ya cerradas, una (W36) sigue bajo el factor de ganancia minimo exigido (1.18 vs 1.3). El cambio de stop propuesto hace dos semanas sigue sin aplicarse en TradingView, con cuatro segmentos ya confirmados de forma solida y un quinto (2m BUY RETEST) acercandose a su segunda confirmacion seguida. Vigilar: en SELL RETEST 1m, la regla 'el simbolo CL rinde mal' que se venia reportando por varios dias se revirtio del todo al crecer la muestra -- recordatorio de no fijar reglas todavia con muestra chica.",
    "en": "Today we measured 13095 signal+outcome pairs for Scalp CC (1643 new since yesterday; 37 pending, 32 outcomes with no matching signal -- the orphan count rose but stayed stable relative to the size of the new data batch, no clear sign of a new pipeline problem, still worth watching). On average each trade gains 0.055 times what was risked, with the 90% confidence interval (0.037 to 0.073) not crossing zero -- the system keeps winning overall, a bit better than yesterday (0.049). Overall win rate 46.2%. The main cause of stop-outs remains a target set too close to the stop (RR-too-low), which today separates clearly as the dominant cause in BUY RETEST (it was nearly tied with another cause before). The managed entry-ladder-plus-partials approach keeps beating the simple one (+0.074 difference). Today's most important finding: the 1m BUY RETEST segment gained a statistically real edge for the first time (its confidence interval used to graze zero), joining 5m as the two LONG segments with solid evidence. On the execution ladder: we remain at advisor level (rung 0) -- 5m BUY RETEST meets all four minimum gate numbers, but of the two already-closed weeks, one (W36) still falls short of the minimum profit factor required (1.18 vs 1.3). The stop-loss change proposed two weeks ago still hasn't been applied in TradingView, with four segments now solidly confirmed and a fifth (2m BUY RETEST) approaching its second consecutive confirmation. Watch item: in SELL RETEST 1m, the 'symbol CL underperforms' rule that had been reported for several days reversed completely as the sample grew -- a reminder not to lock in rules on small samples yet."
  },
